# Atomic identity adoption source draft

This source is inactive until qualified facade main, exact provider pins, reviewed CAP16 data and root admission are complete.
The loader whole-pins actual D/G/C/H/F before execution; its facade pin remains PENDING until root records qualified bytes.
The compatibility module aliases the real facade; old .10/.8 and identity .11 views stay distinct. Actual current tests read the physical .12 root.
Root owns the fixed derive/norm/generator/snapshot entry, manual seals, data, locks, briefs and CI. Expected-plan data never replaces actual generator output.
Original CAP16 bodies remain historical data; these phase adapters are applied only with atomic .12 source and normative lock adoption.
All old cases and new actual-loader controls remain mandatory in normal and optimized modes. Source presence grants no execution or feature acceptance.
Actual source/proof lineage, sufficientN<=62 proofs and full64MiB composition must be independently qualified; no cap increase or proof pruning.
Parent functional/measurement/native/UI/backend gates and ownership holds remain open.
